    "updated_at": "2018-12-10T09:55:17Z",
    "body": "See also #106. I think we mostly want object identity here, except for primitive data types. Most specifications already assume those semantics when it comes to equality.\r\n\r\nI think the second sentence doesn't really relate to the first that much and probably needs to be reworded. Maybe something like:\r\n\r\n> For a list _list_ and an index _index_, _list_[_index_] exists, if _index_ is not out-of-bound for _list_.",
