    "created_at": "2018-12-10T10:54:58Z",
    "updated_at": "2018-12-10T10:54:58Z",
    "body": "Some definitions in Infra are fairly vacuous. E.g. contains delegates to an undefined \"appears in\" concept, iterate to \"on each item in order\", append and prepend to \"add\". The intention is roughly \"you already know what this vague concept is, but here's the exact word you can use and reference\".\r\n\r\nWe could probably redefine \"contains\" in terms of equals and iterate, instead of \"appears\". But I'm not sure how far we should pursue such a program. The endpoint of making these definitions rigorous is basically axiomatic set theory.",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
